    </p>
    <p>
      What I care most about isn't the tooling — it's how the work gets done. Good data engineering happens <strong>in close collaboration with the business units</strong> that depend on it. The job isn't to ship pipelines; it's to build trust and a shared understanding of the underlying problem. Every dbt model, every Dagster asset, every schema decision should trace back to a real question someone in the business is trying to answer.
    </p>
